WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.162
Let's extend the sales project beyond simple totals.

00:00:03.162 --> 00:00:07.397
First, we calculate month-to-month growth for the first product.

00:00:07.397 --> 00:00:11.692
N P dot diff calculates the difference between consecutive values.

00:00:11.692 --> 00:00:18.482
We divide those differences by the previous month's value to convert the change into a relative growth rate.

00:00:18.482 --> 00:00:22.462
Click Run and look at the three growth values.

00:00:22.462 --> 00:00:25.447
Four monthly sales values produce three month-to-month changes.

00:00:25.447 --> 00:00:30.752
Then we calculate standard deviation across each product row using axis one.

00:00:30.752 --> 00:00:35.487
This gives us a measure of how much each product's monthly sales vary.

00:00:35.487 --> 00:00:41.452
A higher standard deviation means the values fluctuate more across the observed months.

00:00:41.452 --> 00:00:46.827
The important professional lesson is that NumPy produces numerical summaries,

00:00:46.827 --> 00:00:49.592
but the analyst must explain their meaning.

00:00:49.592 --> 00:00:54.427
A result such as zero point one two growth is not just a number.

00:00:54.427 --> 00:00:59.072
It represents approximately twelve percent growth from one month to the next.
